#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ec5627a-4a37-5a14-9b39-1b43b422171f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex and Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "d7d8ce77-98d8-54d6-9684-edde0ba9e1ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-1450" :question/problem "For the parabola shown below, find the vertex and the equation of the axis of symmetry.\n\n![](images/e8/e88db5363a50530228fefa2e69a9a3a0e1a62eb461103441e61af5c1f7eb6c3b.png)" :question/worked-solution "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In a downwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the maximum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(-2,3).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=-2.$\n\n![](images/91/91e9d323945b1520aa36b70f3faf8c801e28b21437cd1008b54e76dae76d5ccb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "7b9c1bbd-6d33-5fb8-a207-02cf71ba8b0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-1451" :question/problem "Find the roots of the parabola shown below.\n\n![](images/87/87ed924d518696b8d9f442df341700aab36b8bedfbdee88269c94e54eb8a4478.png)" :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola. \n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-2,0)$ and $(4,0).$ \n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "867af724-0aa0-599a-8a5f-ee753fd19414" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Parabola Given Its Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "d43441ff-4ab3-5cfd-ad5d-fbb6f82fa504" :question/math-academy-id "e-1452" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=-x^2+4x-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=-x^2+4x-3.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=0,1,2,3,4$ and then use the formula $y=-x^2+4x-3$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-3$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/44/442d3550eb77f837da6875bc3877023db44f9f3ee862b433fa56d2186c352bd2.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/e9/e95ebb53e7924dc1e99a92be85e6981def3c1186029c6c620bded4bb797f0c06.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae1738d1-3261-5769-ab80-0edcc76ab6f3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Y-Intercept of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "5bb6861a-ea00-5644-bc16-d458cd2bb30f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7375" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e012ecda75df732e1c96ea4a52762fb085f444f41991ed9a3fe72d7d8e10025.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y=x^2+2x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+2x+k \\\\ y & =(0)^{2}+2(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=0$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $\\left(0,0\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ec5627a-4a37-5a14-9b39-1b43b422171f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex and Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "179ea49a-2fe6-598c-98e3-82ebaa8f23c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(6,5)$, line of symmetry: $x=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528360} {:answer/id #uuid "20a1c38f-14d0-54c2-aa1b-27992356d597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(5,6)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528388} {:answer/id #uuid "49182a1a-d1a2-5516-844d-c2cbd63c579b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(5,6)$, line of symmetry: $x=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528483} {:answer/id #uuid "5be5250d-98eb-544c-bd07-c52401dbba56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(5,-6)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528517} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa5f12a-3886-539c-b393-38d2c6a11432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(6,5)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20a1c38f-14d0-54c2-aa1b-27992356d597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(5,6)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528388} :answer-field/id #uuid "e979b5aa-d854-5946-b2f2-b44451a4405d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a174f7c-09d0-50e5-afac-66bf0cc4c315" :question/math-academy-id "q-106029" :question/problem "![](images/68/687ea4a6fac8c4c6b7df7336f13b8ca39eb1b7049990c9875eeeaf556bd5353c.png)\n\nFor the parabola shown above, find the vertex and the equation of the axis of symmetry." :question/worked-solution "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In an upwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the maximum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(5,6).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=5.$\n\n![](images/ed/ed00e2896127e6f3da7fc8e63c22e1944434060ac53e4e63d31f1cd7590a8627.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71221b89-0e4a-5c2b-bc88-3d846a415acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528566} {:answer/id #uuid "bdac80d4-23d5-5508-be12-8819ce04d371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-5$ and $x=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528763} {:answer/id #uuid "cec52289-e463-54ce-875c-563a27e4c4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-5$ and $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528808} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c268f8-b35a-53a8-bc9f-0fc1248085da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-5$ and $x=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528831} {:answer/id #uuid "f5aaed55-ac20-50e6-8c01-664268febc9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$ and $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdac80d4-23d5-5508-be12-8819ce04d371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-5$ and $x=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528763} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9e6ff9-aea3-5884-90a2-d4e33d398c8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba657a54-9357-5409-90cb-ee552f02dde2" :question/math-academy-id "q-106037" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc388ceccdd95990d69ebf1c2df36ab8ed0c83228d7684b13a7a791e9705851f.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-5$ and $x=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125aaca2-8199-5cdb-b3d6-125f68a8887d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528343} {:answer/id #uuid "471e6ebe-690c-5c26-bbff-d8d4badef082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528478} {:answer/id #uuid "4ecbe803-d6d2-5446-92a8-59987f4249af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528494} {:answer/id #uuid "d35956cf-9d9d-5176-bfe3-be7be73354d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528827} {:answer/id #uuid "fb28c997-2af0-5dab-a9d1-0a965fd9a82c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d35956cf-9d9d-5176-bfe3-be7be73354d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528827} :answer-field/id #uuid "be1534b1-2d47-5d83-8a64-485245d75f7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a08fd8f-f28b-522d-892c-2595551ed22c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106039" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e207974b8c7b872864cce6e3ef80335ed0c9d20ec1b10960d36fb6a86971878.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve does not intercept the $x$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the parabola does not have any roots."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae1738d1-3261-5769-ab80-0edcc76ab6f3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Y-Intercept of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac7d6e1-050b-59bb-8459-6b9fce755995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528326} {:answer/id #uuid "46525a5c-083e-57ca-a9c6-230718510f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528476} {:answer/id #uuid "654e1f9b-f174-5aa1-910d-781435311218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528541} {:answer/id #uuid "9811c8d3-c957-52fb-9b1d-e16c0bfa96be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528660} {:answer/id #uuid "9aab5299-31bb-531a-9577-a930edf4db8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aab5299-31bb-531a-9577-a930edf4db8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528671} :answer-field/id #uuid "36426514-7bc1-54d9-8654-f61d7bab9bb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1100bf2f-961a-5344-8257-63842e33b322" :question/math-academy-id "q-106044" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cf3840cca56d90bc6b3981d15ead9c4ae45665693ef5c7794e65574204e632db.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y={x}^{2}-3x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-3x+k \\\\ y & =(0)^{2}-3(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=2$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae1738d1-3261-5769-ab80-0edcc76ab6f3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Y-Intercept of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f04964f-2301-566c-83e7-ae340242fcf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528523} {:answer/id #uuid "78a884a3-002e-58a6-8b69-66e3e9cdad98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528581} {:answer/id #uuid "a0079827-2b4a-51cb-9347-a6b433588055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528684} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d3ffe3-cd09-5c51-bd49-d72e9c2d9ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528897} {:answer/id #uuid "fb89a373-134a-511e-bb9e-a5f83a1aa2b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0079827-2b4a-51cb-9347-a6b433588055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528684} :answer-field/id #uuid "49340bef-7c0d-5a21-aca5-48fc9e33b5f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4cc27684-d306-5b1a-a65f-84d96866a22e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106046" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd847efd8b91b1c622e93b1ee97035bcee803a79a603aa7b4beee8fae77abf06.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y=-{x}^{2}+2x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}-x+k \\\\ y & =-(0)^{2}+2(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=5$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "867af724-0aa0-599a-8a5f-ee753fd19414" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Parabola Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f8b5c5-5a79-5789-bffa-95fbf9c0cca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c956047bf140923ce38416d6f70374c94c37ae1c067584ced3ba4c831f036360.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528323} {:answer/id #uuid "0ff3f3c4-60a4-5f30-a928-24d65afeda4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7f2bd4a766b0acd0ddfa4c613b8b145cfc1065c2bd68bd4225262c998cd85f3a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528336} {:answer/id #uuid "665a8330-259b-54cb-824e-dff4c4b69374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a4e843aecb4855baad729fc9c1864ae19ab95733bd89396605a9544b241258f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528544} {:answer/id #uuid "7a9cd5f1-cfb7-5a25-b73f-89d2328ab9d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24aae5c27fc48b7a340e36f6a54d9d6d636644c938e5328c1a8c68713179a947.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528587} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb6008b-4190-517a-b2e2-2c5b4ac708ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a4/a44c42c06b2dd3c2465910498ea1f74632f1adc85b23d527e9596e73499f8d23.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a9cd5f1-cfb7-5a25-b73f-89d2328ab9d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24aae5c27fc48b7a340e36f6a54d9d6d636644c938e5328c1a8c68713179a947.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528587} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c217e0-5a36-5f19-a946-f15d4311ad3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57d98e6f-6b53-5ed4-abd4-c02ceb5b88f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-106054" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y=-{x}^{2}+10x-28?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=-{x}^{2}+10x-28.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=3,4,5,6,7,8,$ and then use the formula $y=-{x}^{2}+10x-28$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $-7$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-7$ | $-12$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/b7/b762d214dbd72555b069846ca8e7bcb5248c73c15db10f06018167ff7966d6d0.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/24/24aae5c27fc48b7a340e36f6a54d9d6d636644c938e5328c1a8c68713179a947.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529123 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "867af724-0aa0-599a-8a5f-ee753fd19414" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Parabola Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "275c3b78-1f78-5062-a1b1-5603932f8c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b9a8459c307939f7b95290217f8d98ce23a1e9317706adf8e5c4761d225e34ab.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528401} {:answer/id #uuid "52d72a9e-8d18-5223-88c1-28fe8f4dfaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/75/7575e4eaecb7e5a84397b0a0a9b9661f6f83db71a0304c2e2e31e3ab42ec801d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528499} {:answer/id #uuid "56f9ea1a-984f-5c8f-9d69-f76de09e5137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8d/8de7d3c268e35f85da8f1bf7882d2ebd285fa3f5c0c239c986eeb1564277e4e1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528506} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba4edf5-3a2e-5873-bbde-115b6a4cb0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6d/6d5eaff1bbe70dc963ca08e2bfddeab05d8dbd61df68fe85f3545ee979d969be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528559} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8f322d-12cf-527b-9535-e15eef757d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/62/622f81fb3304e6300fa0c82d8c540685268e9fde56c8a6e986edc3f788ef54db.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56f9ea1a-984f-5c8f-9d69-f76de09e5137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8d/8de7d3c268e35f85da8f1bf7882d2ebd285fa3f5c0c239c986eeb1564277e4e1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528506} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb700264-272d-54a5-aa96-05b215519e4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53ebdab8-abca-5063-be77-653bbbd15d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106057" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,$ and then use the formula $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $3$ | $13$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/b4/b43e0f6b6f359b08dd346a30509d82482a3b82defac90728ddaa7c9769690846.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/8d/8de7d3c268e35f85da8f1bf7882d2ebd285fa3f5c0c239c986eeb1564277e4e1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ec5627a-4a37-5a14-9b39-1b43b422171f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vertex and Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d276868-fe6b-507d-8ab9-43180ad9fccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(2,3)$, line of symmetry: $x=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528492} {:answer/id #uuid "4f277e75-74ce-54d2-9035-15a37f995d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(-2,3)$, line of symmetry: $y=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528495} {:answer/id #uuid "890cbcbb-a92b-5d7c-8d74-969403bf22bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(3,-2)$, line of symmetry: $x=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528628} {:answer/id #uuid "c8731d7b-9b13-5a37-a523-9ea5e0ef05e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(3,-2)$, line of symmetry: $x=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528790} {:answer/id #uuid "cd58fa58-4a48-5b20-a716-a9639b6de6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(3,2)$, line of symmetry: $y=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "890cbcbb-a92b-5d7c-8d74-969403bf22bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vertex: $(3,-2)$, line of symmetry: $x=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528628} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae76a4c4-d817-58c1-9753-810921f0228b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6ba3114-4b55-54d8-a439-a9e561cd3410" :question/math-academy-id "q-24393" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f57f1223c28fc554909be6bbd2e8eafefa21a886b1a5abb47549f17bfa12e2ab.png)\n\nFor the parabola shown above, find the vertex and the equation of the axis of symmetry." :question/worked-solution "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In an upwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the minimum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(3,-2).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=3.$\n\n![](images/f1/f139192260875d5e988f30a64a7024f50d68337dbd4969d938f18aa62b850dd0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17352e86-0ea3-5ff1-ac23-83fc70c2755d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528357} {:answer/id #uuid "344dff3f-79ef-5bf1-9898-8954bbe773d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528429} {:answer/id #uuid "485c2fcc-535a-5c6d-9f0e-184dbf6a2092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528480} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d666f9-4d9b-5b92-b0d9-4b160d8e16c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528687} {:answer/id #uuid "f828c12c-4f0d-5260-bc18-c3e137461a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "344dff3f-79ef-5bf1-9898-8954bbe773d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528429} :answer-field/id #uuid "d70f01f2-7346-5a78-be2c-b05e2ed37264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1834012f-4a0b-5e03-8f32-bee5b9948e5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-24639" :question/problem "![](images/28/28032a665a1266f06292394bc9a238b196c25ef9e8d275009e3d7587a1511c6e.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the point $(-1,0).$\n\nTherefore, the root is $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb0d9a4-9047-58f4-8e38-7b273aec2f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528335} {:answer/id #uuid "17b63a5e-4d4f-59d2-bcf5-ef6faf036147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528362} {:answer/id #uuid "20178d11-ebc0-5da0-843f-8cc3f52ecea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528386} {:answer/id #uuid "48772eb0-5236-582d-9569-8f9cf2ff0769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528482} {:answer/id #uuid "f474f41c-02ad-500d-a513-2b1e0c39ae6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb0d9a4-9047-58f4-8e38-7b273aec2f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528335} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c31abc-c57f-5d89-acd3-ebe0893ace11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8dc19dd-4912-57fc-b7e0-84c553fa7c79" :question/math-academy-id "q-30782" :question/problem "![](images/05/05213dec3ea87b199cdd6c4bd73f5dedc3e19df69fed5ceef4a44dda60365b4b.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$ axis at the points $(3,0)$ and $(6,0).$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=3$ and $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae1738d1-3261-5769-ab80-0edcc76ab6f3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Y-Intercept of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165ecd6b-2ac4-5fd1-8c73-a2644c7f185d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528356} {:answer/id #uuid "780a86b0-806e-5172-9848-d1df1932bb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528578} {:answer/id #uuid "80de2eb0-6caf-5df9-8c58-692b1d2bc75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528608} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ce0898-747d-5c52-bd5f-3c34f462a124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528771} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5c6042-a815-5608-beed-8a21ca8c1365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "780a86b0-806e-5172-9848-d1df1932bb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528578} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a36c5be-bb58-5992-90d2-1b9b6c33f67b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fffc2429-ebec-5416-9ec6-594433fbf3de" :question/math-academy-id "q-83561" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca545b153cd04a539f30030c27a90dc4489b3a620e9a0d859bae5b531fcc7144.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y=\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}-3x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}-3x+k \\\\ y & =\\frac{5}{2}(0)^{2}-3(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=\\frac{1}{2}$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$"}]}
